# 🚀 Development Workflow - TaskMaster + Memory + Context Framework

## **🎯 MANDATORY DEVELOPMENT PATTERN**

### **Every Development Session MUST Follow This 6-Step Flow:**

```typescript
// 1. TASK CONTEXT: Get current task and search existing knowledge
const currentTask = mcp_taskmaster-ai_next_task()
const relatedNodes = mcp_graphiti-memory_search_memory_nodes(currentTask.title)
const relatedFacts = mcp_graphiti-memory_search_memory_facts(currentTask.description)
const similarPatterns = mcp_qdrant_qdrant-find(`similar to ${currentTask.description}`)

// 2. SYSTEM CONTEXT: Query current system state
const systemState = mcp_neo4j-cypher_execute_query("MATCH (n) RETURN n LIMIT 10")
const currentData = postgres-mes-local.query("SELECT * FROM relevant_table LIMIT 10")

// 3. IMPLEMENTATION: Code the solution
// ... your implementation work ...

// 4. MEMORY UPDATE: Document in knowledge graph (MANDATORY)
mcp_graphiti-memory_add_memory({
  name: `Implementation: ${currentTask.title}`,
  episode_body: `
    Task: ${currentTask.title}
    Approach: [specific technical approach]
    Files modified: [list of files]
    Key decisions: [architectural choices]
    Integration points: [systems connected]
    Patterns established: [reusable patterns]
  `,
  source: "text"
})

// 5. VECTOR STORAGE: Store searchable patterns
mcp_qdrant_qdrant-store({
  information: `Solution: ${currentTask.title} implemented using [approach] with [key patterns]`,
  metadata: { 
    task_id: currentTask.id,
    type: "implementation",
    component: "ComponentName"
  }
})

// 6. TASK COMPLETION: Update task status
mcp_taskmaster-ai_set_task_status({
  id: currentTask.id,
  status: "done"
})
```

## **📋 Development Workflow Phases**

### **Phase 1: Session Initialization (MANDATORY)**

```typescript
// A. Get Current Task Context
const nextTask = mcp_taskmaster-ai_next_task()
// OR: const tasks = mcp_taskmaster-ai_get_tasks({status: "pending"})

// B. Search Knowledge Graph for Related Entities
const relatedEntities = mcp_graphiti-memory_search_memory_nodes(nextTask.title)
const relatedFacts = mcp_graphiti-memory_search_memory_facts(nextTask.description)

// C. Find Similar Patterns in Vector Database
const similarPatterns = mcp_qdrant_qdrant-find(`implementation patterns for ${nextTask.description}`)

// D. Query Current System State
const systemSchema = mcp_neo4j-cypher_execute_query("MATCH (n:Table) RETURN n.name")
const currentData = postgres-mes-local.query("SELECT * FROM relevant_table LIMIT 10")

// E. Check Infrastructure Status (Optional)
const containerStatus = mcp_MCP_DOCKER.listContainers()
```

### **Phase 2: Task Analysis & Planning**

```typescript
// A. Analyze Task Complexity
const complexityAnalysis = mcp_taskmaster-ai_analyze_project_complexity({
  ids: nextTask.id,
  research: true
})

// B. Expand Complex Tasks if Needed
if (complexityAnalysis.score > 5) {
  mcp_taskmaster-ai_expand_task({
    id: nextTask.id,
    research: true,
    force: true
  })
}

// C. Document Planning Phase
mcp_graphiti-memory_add_memory({
  name: `Planning: ${nextTask.title}`,
  episode_body: `
    Task analysis: [complexity findings]
    Implementation strategy: [planned approach]
    Dependencies identified: [system dependencies]
    Risk assessment: [potential challenges]
  `,
  source: "text"
})
```

### **Phase 3: Implementation (CONTINUOUS DOCUMENTATION)**

```typescript
// A. Start Implementation
mcp_taskmaster-ai_set_task_status({
  id: nextTask.id,
  status: "in-progress"
})

// B. Code Implementation
// ... your actual coding work ...

// C. Document Progress (DO THIS FREQUENTLY)
mcp_taskmaster-ai_update_task({
  id: nextTask.id,
  prompt: `
    Progress update: [current status]
    Discoveries: [new findings]
    Challenges: [obstacles encountered]
    Solutions: [approaches taken]
    Next steps: [planned actions]
  `
})

// D. Update Knowledge Graph During Implementation
mcp_graphiti-memory_add_memory({
  name: `${nextTask.title} - Implementation Progress`,
  episode_body: `
    Phase: Implementation
    Files modified: [specific files]
    Architectural decisions: [key choices made]
    Integration points: [systems connected]
    Performance considerations: [optimization notes]
    Testing approach: [validation strategy]
  `,
  source: "text"
})
```

### **Phase 4: Cross-System Integration Documentation**

```typescript
// A. Document System Integration Points
mcp_graphiti-memory_add_memory({
  name: "System Integration Point",
  episode_body: JSON.stringify({
    component: "ComponentName",
    database_tables: ["table1", "table2"],
    api_endpoints: ["/api/endpoint"],
    business_process: "ProcessName",
    implementation_details: "specific technical approach",
    related_tasks: [nextTask.id],
    integration_type: "database|api|ui|business_logic"
  }),
  source: "json"
})

// B. Store Reusable Patterns
mcp_qdrant_qdrant-store({
  information: `Integration pattern: ${component} connects to [systems] via [method] for [purpose]`,
  metadata: {
    type: "integration_pattern",
    component: "ComponentName",
    systems: ["database", "api", "ui"],
    task_id: nextTask.id
  }
})
```

### **Phase 5: Testing & Validation**

```typescript
// A. UI Testing with Playwright (when applicable)
playwright.goto("http://localhost:3000/feature-url")
playwright.click("[data-testid='feature-button']")
playwright.waitForSelector("[data-testid='success-indicator']")

// B. Validate Database Changes
const validationResult = postgres-mes-local.query(`
  SELECT * FROM ${affectedTable} 
  WHERE ${validationCondition}
`)

// C. Document Testing Results
mcp_graphiti-memory_add_memory({
  name: `Testing: ${nextTask.title}`,
  episode_body: `
    Test scenarios: [what was tested]
    UI validation: [user interface testing]
    Database validation: [data integrity checks]
    Integration testing: [cross-system validation]
    Performance testing: [performance metrics]
    Edge cases: [boundary conditions tested]
  `,
  source: "text"
})
```

### **Phase 6: Completion & Knowledge Consolidation**

```typescript
// A. Final Implementation Documentation
mcp_graphiti-memory_add_memory({
  name: `Feature Complete: ${nextTask.title}`,
  episode_body: JSON.stringify({
    feature: nextTask.title,
    implementation_approach: "detailed technical approach",
    components_created: ["Component1", "Component2"],
    apis_integrated: ["/api/endpoint1", "/api/endpoint2"],
    database_changes: ["table1", "table2"],
    business_value: "specific business outcome",
    testing_strategy: "how feature was validated",
    deployment_notes: "deployment considerations",
    lessons_learned: "key insights for future work"
  }),
  source: "json"
})

// B. Store Final Patterns for Future Use
mcp_qdrant_qdrant-store({
  information: `Complete solution: ${nextTask.title} - [summary of approach and key patterns]`,
  metadata: {
    type: "complete_solution",
    feature: nextTask.title,
    complexity: complexityAnalysis.score,
    patterns: ["pattern1", "pattern2"],
    task_id: nextTask.id
  }
})

// C. Update Task Status
mcp_taskmaster-ai_set_task_status({
  id: nextTask.id,
  status: "done"
})

// D. Generate Task Files (if needed)
mcp_taskmaster-ai_generate()
```

